# Command: AI (Set frame(s))
# Radio: Kenwood TS-480HX / TS-480SAT
# Title (cover, verbatim): "PC CONTROL COMMAND REFERENCE FOR THE TS-480HX/ SAT
#   TRANSCEIVER"
# Printed revision: NONE printed; cover carries "KENWOOD CORPORATION",
#   "(c) 2003/11/28" and the printing code line "09 08 07 06 05 04 03 02 01 00".
# Source page: printed folio "3"  ==  PDF page 4 of 26
# Charts used: the Set chart of the AI block (Read and Answer charts recorded below
#   for completeness of the position map)
# Derivation date: 05/09/2026
# NO code, no generator, no other file and no other document was consulted.
#
# COUNTED FRAME LENGTHS (two independent counts of the printed numbered ruler):
#   AI Set    = 4 positions
#   AI Read   = 3 positions
#   AI Answer = 4 positions
#   (identical to the TS-590 book's AI lengths)
#
# CHARTS, position by position:
#   Set:     1 A  2 I  3 P1  4 ;      (5..10 empty)
#   Read:    1 A  2 I  3 ;            (4..10 empty)
#   Answer:  1 A  2 I  3 P1  4 ;      (5..10 empty)
#
# Field map (Set):
#   pos 1-2  "AI"
#   pos 3    P1  (one character)
#   pos 4    ";"
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LEGEND, VERBATIM (the complete right-hand column; block description reads
# "Sets or reads the Auto Information (AI) function ON/ OFF."):
#
#   Parameters:
#   P1
#     0: AI OFF
#     1: Only old AI format is ON
#     2: Only extended AI format is ON
#     3: Both formats are ON
#
#   When the extended AI format is selected, the transceiver
#   automatically sends the parameters.
#   When the old AI is ON and the IF parameters change, the
#   transceiver sends the IF command every 1.5 seconds.
#   When the transceiver is turned OFF, the AI parameter
#   becomes 0.
#
#   (Four consecutive values 0,1,2,3 - a DIFFERENT value set and different meanings
#    from the TS-590 book's AI, which prints only 0, 2 and 4.  See FINDING F9.)
#
# POSITIONS THE CHART PRINTS AS FIXED / "Always": NONE in the AI block.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BYTES WHOSE VALUE THE MANUAL DOES NOT DETERMINE  -> INHERITED-ASSUMED
#   NONE.  Every byte of every vector below is determined by the printed chart and
#   the printed legend.
#
# Hardware status: UNVERIFIED for every vector in this file.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VECTORS  (name <TAB> frame bytes verbatim)
#
ai480_set_off	AI0;
ai480_set_old_format_only	AI1;
ai480_set_extended_format_only	AI2;
ai480_set_both_formats	AI3;
ai480_read	AI;
ai480_answer_off	AI0;
ai480_answer_old_format_only	AI1;
ai480_answer_extended_format_only	AI2;
ai480_answer_both_formats	AI3;
